    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-06"
   },
   {
    "quote": "Entity resolution is the method of determining when different records from one or more data sources refer to the same entity. In a corporate context, these entities could be companies, businesses, or other organisations. Entity resolution helps organisations:",
    "url": "https://blog.opencorporates.com/2025/02/03/primary-vs-secondary-identifiers-for-entity-resolution/",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-06"
   },
   {
    "quote": "Entity resolution addresses these risks. It uses strong data matching and classification methods. At the heart of these procedures lie",
    "url": "https://blog.opencorporates.com/2025/02/03/primary-vs-secondary-identifiers-for-entity-resolution/",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-06"
   },
   {
    "quote": ": Assign match confidence scores based on how many primary and secondary identifiers match. This approach ensures a risk-based method, where higher-risk entities face deeper checks.",
    "url": "https://blog.opencorporates.com/2025/02/03/primary-vs-secondary-identifiers-for-entity-resolution/",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-06"
   }
